&lt;p&gt;At GWI we’re always looking for extraordinary people who thrive on making an extraordinary impact. Right now we’re looking for a&lt;strong&gt; Product Manager &lt;/strong&gt;to play a key role in our &lt;strong&gt;User Management (Revenue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;amp; Enablement) &lt;/strong&gt;team in &lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt;. If that’s you, and making a difference gets you out of bed in the morning, keep reading. It could be the start of something, well, extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Sounds great, what will I be doing? 🤔&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Product Manager you&#39;ll own the systems that make GWI&#39;s subscription and consumption business run, such as billing, metering, user plans, feature access, product analytics and user messaging. It&#39;s the layer everything else sits on. Get it right and GWI can price, package and sell in new ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two big pieces of work sit at the heart of this role. The first is billing for our consumption products, which is an area we&#39;re actively developing, and one you&#39;ll help shape. The second is making our internal tools talk to each other properly, so user data flows consistently between them and Salesforce, and everyone across the business is working from the same picture. Most of your stakeholders are internal - Revenue Operations, Finance, Business Intelligence, Client Success and Engineering - with some direct client contact along the way. You&#39;ll lead one squad of front-end and back-end engineers and a designer, alongside the PM and Engineers in our sister squad, Identity &amp;amp; Access - together you cover the whole of User Management.&lt;/p&gt;
